<item>
            <title>[LU-20892] nodemap: exp_banned write without exp_lock can lose exp_hashed</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20892</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Problem&lt;br/&gt;
nodemap writes exp_banned without exp_lock. exp_banned is a 1-bit field in the same word as exp_hashed and other export flags. The struct comment says that exp_lock protects that word. A concurrent write to another bit in the word can lose the exp_banned update, or the exp_banned write can lose the other update.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Environment&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master at 550451c0e4 and earlier.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A server with nodemap active.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Reproduction&lt;br/&gt;
Source analysis only. We did not reproduce the failure.&lt;br/&gt;
1. A client connects. target_handle_connect() calls obd_nid_add(), which sets exp_hashed.&lt;br/&gt;
2. At the same time, a nodemap change calls nm_member_reclassify_nodemap(), which sets or clears exp_banned on the same export.&lt;br/&gt;
3. Each side reads the word, changes its bit, and writes the word back. The later write removes the earlier update.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Analysis&lt;br/&gt;
Writers of exp_banned without exp_lock:&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;nodemap_add_member(), lustre/ptlrpc/nodemap_handler.c&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;nm_member_reclassify_nodemap(), the &quot;banning client&quot; and &quot;un-banned client&quot; branches, lustre/ptlrpc/nodemap_member.c&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The two results of a lost update:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;exp_hashed goes back to 0 while the export is in obd_nid_hash. class_disconnect() then skips obd_nid_del(), and the hash keeps its export reference. The export leaks.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;exp_banned goes back to its old value. The ban change does not apply.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20403&quot; title=&quot;Refresh import conn on primary migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20403&quot;&gt;LU-20403&lt;/a&gt; adds a runtime writer of exp_hashed: ptlrpc_refresh_export_primary() re-keys the export in obd_nid_hash under exp_lock when the client primary NID migrates. Before &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20403&quot; title=&quot;Refresh import conn on primary migration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20403&quot;&gt;LU-20403&lt;/a&gt;, the main writer ran at connect.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Proposed fix&lt;br/&gt;
Take exp_lock around each exp_banned write in nodemap_handler.c and nodemap_member.c.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
